      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 2.88,
          "en": "That's how nested routes work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.88,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "Now of course, I also wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 9.27,
          "en": "that we can reach them through links in our user interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.27,
          "end": 12.48,
          "en": "so that we don't have to manually update the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.48,
          "end": 14.943,
          "en": "because again, no one does that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.17,
          "end": 20.34,
          "en": "So as a first step, we should go to the user component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.34,
          "end": 24.27,
          "en": "because there we have the link to /users, slash some ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.27,
          "end": 27.48,
          "en": "Well there this link should actually be updated now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.48,
          "end": 30.37,
          "en": "and also have tasks at the end here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.23,
          "end": 33.45,
          "en": "so that we create a link that leads",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.45,
          "end": 37.503,
          "en": "to /users, slash some ID /tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.57,
          "end": 43.08,
          "en": "In addition, in that user tasks component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.08,
          "end": 45.99,
          "en": "where I have this add task link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.99,
          "end": 48.06,
          "en": "I also want to activate that link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.06,
          "end": 51.45,
          "en": "by using the router link directive here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.45,
          "end": 55.23,
          "en": "And that should now navigate to /users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.23,
          "end": 60.003,
          "en": "Then the idea of the active user /tasks /new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.59,
          "end": 64.23,
          "en": "Now, we could try to construct it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.23,
          "end": 66.66,
          "en": "and for that we would need to get hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.66,
          "end": 68.01,
          "en": "of the user ID somehow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.01,
          "end": 70.98,
          "en": "and construct this string dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.98,
          "end": 74.07,
          "en": "But conveniently, Angular also allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.07,
          "end": 76.143,
          "en": "to set up relative links,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.34,
          "end": 79.41,
          "en": "and that's what I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.41,
          "end": 81.42,
          "en": "This is now a relative link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.42,
          "end": 85.44,
          "en": "relative to the currently activated route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.44,
          "end": 90.44,
          "en": "So this user tasks component belongs to this route here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.17,
          "end": 93.69,
          "en": "So any links you define in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.69,
          "end": 96.96000000000001,
          "en": "are relative to this route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.96000000000001,
          "end": 100.22999999999999,
          "en": "So they are appended to the currently active path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.22999999999999,
          "end": 103.443,
          "en": "which would be users, slash some id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.67,
          "end": 108.9,
          "en": "That's why here we can simply construct this relative path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.9,
          "end": 111.72,
          "en": "and as a result we'll get the full path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.72,
          "end": 115.19,
          "en": "to /users, slash the ID of the currently active user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.19,
          "end": 117.87299999999999,
          "en": "/tasks /new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.22,
          "end": 121.92,
          "en": "With that, you of course also must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.92,
          "end": 125.4,
          "en": "that in the user tasks component TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.4,
          "end": 127.77,
          "en": "you import router link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.77,
          "end": 129.933,
          "en": "and you add it to this imports array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.12,
          "end": 133.74,
          "en": "With that, if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.74,
          "end": 137.01,
          "en": "you'll see that if you navigate between different users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.01,
          "end": 140.02,
          "en": "tasks is Appendant here in the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.27,
          "end": 143.22,
          "en": "and if you click on add task,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.22,
          "end": 145.38,
          "en": "this form here is loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.38,
          "end": 147.87,
          "en": "because we navigate it to /users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.87,
          "end": 151.38,
          "en": "slash some ID, /tasks /new,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.38,
